{"day":"2026-10-21","number":12,"rounds":[{"facts":[{"text":"Germany built two merchant submarines in World War I to trade for valuable raw materials with the United States.","sources":[{"title":"Germany","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany"},{"title":"Merchant submarine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merchant_submarine"},{"title":"World War I","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_I"},{"title":"United States","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States"}]},{"text":"On February 9, 1913, a procession of fireballs seen across Canada to Brazil likely represented the break-up of a short-lived natural satellite of the Earth.","sources":[{"title":"February 9","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_9"},{"title":"1913","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1913"},{"title":"1913 Great Meteor Procession","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1913_Great_Meteor_Procession"},{"title":"Canada","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada"},{"title":"Brazil","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazil"},{"title":"Natural satellite","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_satellite"}]},{"text":"Ipswich Town won the Football League First Division in their 1961–62 season having been promoted from the Second Division the previous season.","sources":[{"title":"Ipswich Town F.C.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipswich_Town_F.C."},{"title":"Football League First Division","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Football_League_First_Division"},{"title":"1961–62 Ipswich Town F.C. season","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961%E2%80%9362_Ipswich_Town_F.C._season"},{"title":"Football League Second Division","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Football_League_Second_Division"}]},{"text":"Contrary to popular myth, Robert E. Lee's face is not carved on the back of the 1920 statue of Abraham Lincoln in the Lincoln Memorial, Washington D.C.","sources":[{"title":"Robert E. Lee","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_E._Lee"},{"title":"Statue of Abraham Lincoln (Lincoln Memorial)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statue_of_Abraham_Lincoln_(Lincoln_Memorial)"},{"title":"Lincoln Memorial","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincoln_Memorial"},{"title":"Washington, D.C.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington,_D.C."}]},{"text":"Horween Leather Company makes the National Football League's footballs, colloquially known as \"pigskins\", out of goat hides.","sources":[{"title":"Horween Leather Company","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horween_Leather_Company"},{"title":"National Football League","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Football_League"},{"title":"Football (ball)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Football_(ball)"}]}],"fake":4,"original":"Horween Leather Company makes the National Football League's footballs, colloquially known as \"pigskins\", out of steer hides.","change":{"kind":"what","old":"steer hides","new":"goat hides","start":113,"end":124},"difficulty":0.6666666666666666,"nli":0.995,"fact_ids":["5cf6ac8a7a56","bf25c167aabd","d0d9a9d90d29","1473917dc7aa","71b8b4815b86"]},{"facts":[{"text":"The Pettakere cave in Indonesia has hand print paintings estimated to be between 35,000 and 40,000 years old.","sources":[{"title":"Caves in the Maros-Pangkep karst","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caves_in_the_Maros-Pangkep_karst"},{"title":"Indonesia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indonesia"}]},{"text":"In 2001, a football match took place on the summit of Nevado Sajama, the highest mountain in Bolivia.","sources":[{"title":"Association football","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Association_football"},{"title":"Nevado Sajama","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nevado_Sajama"},{"title":"Bolivia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolivia"}]},{"text":"Sandwich toasters are sometimes called \"jaffle irons\" in Canada.","sources":[{"title":"Pie iron","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie_iron"},{"title":"Australia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia"}]},{"text":"Richard I's army of Crusaders encountered Saladin's archers, tarantulas, and heat exhaustion on their march to the Battle of Arsuf.","sources":[{"title":"Richard I of England","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_I_of_England"},{"title":"Third Crusade","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Crusade"},{"title":"Saladin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saladin"},{"title":"Tarantula","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarantula"},{"title":"Battle of Arsuf","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Arsuf"}]},{"text":"One of the first items posted through the New York pneumatic tube mail in 1897 was a live cat.","sources":[{"title":"Pneumatic tube mail in New York City","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneumatic_tube_mail_in_New_York_City"},{"title":"Cat","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat"}]}],"fake":2,"original":"Sandwich toasters are sometimes called \"jaffle irons\" in Australia.","change":{"kind":"where","old":"in Australia","new":"in Canada","start":54,"end":66},"difficulty":0.6666666666666666,"nli":0.9737,"fact_ids":["736829de4986","ab5063fcd936","4c39d63f79fd","5dfb7fef4ea0","d35459c039ae"]},{"facts":[{"text":"In 1940, 40 Wall Street in New York City was worth less than its elevators had cost.","sources":[{"title":"40 Wall Street","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/40_Wall_Street"}]},{"text":"In two species of megabat, males have been observed to produce milk.","sources":[{"title":"Megabat","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Megabat"}]},{"text":"Galileo's father Vincenzo Galilei was a noted Italian glassblower.","sources":[{"title":"Galileo Galilei","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galileo_Galilei"},{"title":"Vincenzo Galilei","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vincenzo_Galilei"},{"title":"Italy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy"},{"title":"Lute","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lute"}]},{"text":"A 1944 serial film was the first film appearance of Captain America and the first film appearance of any Marvel Comics character.","sources":[{"title":"Captain America (serial)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_America_(serial)"},{"title":"Captain America in film","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_America_in_film"},{"title":"Marvel Comics","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvel_Comics"}]},{"text":"The supposed lake associated with El Dorado appeared on European maps of Guiana even though no European had seen it.","sources":[{"title":"El Dorado","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Dorado"}]}],"fake":2,"original":"Galileo's father Vincenzo Galilei was a noted Italian lutenist.","change":{"kind":"what","old":"lutenist","new":"glassblower","start":54,"end":62},"difficulty":0.6666666666666666,"nli":0.9412,"fact_ids":["79e6eddd7afc","6e164d01df7a","00358be8a669","861cbaf63e7e","0c500f307480"]},{"facts":[{"text":"Former Chicago Bears chairman Ed McCaskey tried out for Harry James' band, but lost out to Frank Sinatra.","sources":[{"title":"Chicago Bears","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago_Bears"},{"title":"Ed McCaskey","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ed_McCaskey"},{"title":"Harry James","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_James"},{"title":"Frank Sinatra","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Sinatra"}]},{"text":"The village of Kodinji in Kerala, India, where multiple birth is a regular phenomenon, is home to over 204 pairs of twins.","sources":[{"title":"Kodinhi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kodinhi"},{"title":"Kerala","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kerala"},{"title":"India","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India"},{"title":"Multiple birth","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multiple_birth"},{"title":"Twin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twin"}]},{"text":"The Kelly bag, originally a saddle carrier, became a high-priced status symbol after a namesake princess used it to conceal her baby bump from the paparazzi.","sources":[{"title":"Kelly bag","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_bag"},{"title":"Saddle","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saddle"},{"title":"Status symbol","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Status_symbol"},{"title":"Grace Kelly","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grace_Kelly"},{"title":"Pregnancy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pregnancy"}]},{"text":"Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's opera seria Idomeneo is set on the island of Cyprus following the Trojan War.","sources":[{"title":"Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfgang_Amadeus_Mozart"},{"title":"Opera seria","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opera_seria"},{"title":"Idomeneo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idomeneo"},{"title":"Crete","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crete"},{"title":"Trojan War","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trojan_War"}]},{"text":"The Polynesian Rat is used to track human migrations across the Pacific Ocean.","sources":[{"title":"Polynesian rat","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polynesian_rat"},{"title":"Human migration","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_migration"},{"title":"Pacific Ocean","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Ocean"}]}],"fake":3,"original":"Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's opera seria Idomeneo is set on the island of Crete following the Trojan War.","change":{"kind":"where","old":"the island of Crete","new":"the island of Cyprus","start":57,"end":76},"difficulty":0.6666666666666666,"nli":0.997,"fact_ids":["a9fd1d8ae69a","773fe0f9c4ef","2f5cbb2e8529","0d7f095ad8af","40ee387bc740"]},{"facts":[{"text":"Director Nobuhiko Obayashi purposely made the special effects in the Japanese horror comedy film House look unrealistic.","sources":[{"title":"Nobuhiko Obayashi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobuhiko_Obayashi"},{"title":"Special effect","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_effect"},{"title":"Cinema of Japan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinema_of_Japan"},{"title":"House (1977 film)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_(1977_film)"}]},{"text":"The little owl was sacred to the goddess Artemis, from whom it gets the generic name.","sources":[{"title":"Little owl","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_owl"},{"title":"Athena","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Athena"}]},{"text":"The Laotian Rock Rat is a new species of rodent that is unique enough to lead researchers to create a new family of mammals.","sources":[{"title":"Laotian rock rat","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laotian_rock_rat"},{"title":"Rodent","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rodent"},{"title":"Mammal","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mammal"}]},{"text":"Georgia’s capital Tbilisi functioned as the center of an Islamic emirate under the Arab rule from 736 to 1122.","sources":[{"title":"Georgia (country)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgia_(country)"},{"title":"Tbilisi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tbilisi"},{"title":"Islam","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam"},{"title":"Emirate of Tbilisi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Tbilisi"},{"title":"Arabs","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabs"},{"title":"736","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/736"},{"title":"1122","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1122"}]},{"text":"The staircases in the 1891 Monadnock Building in Chicago were the first use of aluminum in a building.","sources":[{"title":"Monadnock Building","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monadnock_Building"},{"title":"Chicago","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago"},{"title":"Aluminium","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aluminium"}]}],"fake":1,"original":"The little owl was sacred to the goddess Athena, from whom it gets the generic name.","change":{"kind":"who","old":"the goddess Athena","new":"the goddess Artemis","start":29,"end":47},"difficulty":0.6666666666666666,"nli":0.996,"fact_ids":["9de799223905","7ff51c9ef07b","b1a076c6e764","1679e0dfffcb","e219a73d6198"]}]}